## A new attempt: why the last one did not end done

**What it is for.** The task's purpose is unchanged. Your card says how the
previous attempt ended; this one is for finding why it fell short and making
the change that cause calls for.

**Hand back.** What the card asks, and in your receipt the cause you found
with what showed it. When nothing localizes the failure, or the change
belongs outside your write scope, write `blocked` with each hypothesis and
what ruled it out under `ruled_out`.

**How it is judged.** By the same check. What tells one cause from another
is yours to choose. The engine gives three comparisons for free: its own
test nearest the failure (a failure the two share is the engine's or the
site's, not the target's); the same prompts under `modeling_v2="off"` and
`"require"`; and one module in isolation against the HuggingFace module,
with the checkpoint's real weights at the shapes the target runs.
